<title>PHILIPPINES: RFC gets Central Bank nod on bank stake.</title>
<headline>RFC gets Central Bank nod on bank stake.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment holding firm RFC Inc said on Thursday it has received approval from the Central Bank for its purchase of a 30 percent stake in Unitrust Development Bank, a small private bank in the Philippines.</p>
<p>In an advisory to the Philippine Stock Exchange, RFC said it had agreed on a price of 45 million pesos for the 30 percent stake in Unitrust.</p>
<p>Grogram Ltd, a unit of MBf Holdings Berhad of Malaysia, is the controlling shareholder of RFC.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
